  "body": "The maintainer said in chat on 2026-11-22: \"PR's with merge-ready cannot have needs-rework at the same time..\"\n\n## The rule today\n`AGENTS.md`, \"Only collaborators' reviews count\": a PR whose current head has a collaborator's change request and also `merge-ready` (or `merge-ready` with `needs-rework`) is a disagreement. `/merge-ready` reports it. \"No agent removes a label. The two collaborators decide on the PR.\"\n\n## The new rule\n1. `merge-ready` and `needs-rework` are never on the same PR.\n2. The person or agent that sets one of the two labels removes the other label in the same step, with one comment that says why.\n3. A disagreement between two collaborators on the same head: `needs-rework` stays and `merge-ready` is removed. An open change request wins. The collaborator who set `merge-ready` gets the comment.\n4. This replaces the text \"No agent removes a label\" for these two labels.\n\n## Files to change\n- `AGENTS.md`: the rule \"Only collaborators' reviews count\" (the disagreement items) and the \"Review labels\" table.\n- `.claude/skills/merge-ready/SKILL.md`\n- `.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md` and the `PR-reviewer` agent file, where they set a review label.\n- `.claude/skills/resolve-conflicts/SKILL.md`\n- Each other skill or agent file that cites the old disagreement text (search for `needs-rework` and `disagreement`).\n\n## Done means\n- The files above state the new rule with the same words in each place.\n- No file keeps the old text for these two labels.\n- The PR body has the line `Process change: yes`. The PR does not edit `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`.\n- If an `xtask` test pins the old text, the test changes with it.\n",
